          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %strong bilimit
            is the type of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limit
            that is appropriate in a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicategory"} bicategory
          %p There are three notable changes when passing from ordinary 1-limits to bilimits:
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                In order to satisfy the
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principle+of+equivalence"} principle of equivalence
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-morphism"} 2-isomorphism
            %li
              %p
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
                of the limit is expressed by an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
                rather than a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijection"} bijection
                of
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
              %ol
                %li
                  %p every other cone over the diagram that commutes up to isomorphism factors through the limit, up to isomorphism, and
                %li
                  %p
                    every transformation
                    %em between
                    cones also factors through a 2-cell in the limit. We will give some examples below.
            %li
              %p
                Since 2-categories are
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched
                over
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
                (this is precise in the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+2-category"} strict
                case, and
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicategory"} weakly
                true otherwise),
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Cat
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weighted+limit"} weighted limit
                = succeed "-cells" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
                = succeed "-cells." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category+theory"} 2-category theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+2-limit"} strict 2-limit
            (bilimits in 2-categories can be expressed as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+2-limits"} strict 2-limits
            for appropriate weights).
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            be
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicategories"} bicategories
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi D
                  %mo →
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J\colon D\to Cat
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi D
                  %mo →
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F\colon D\to K
            be
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudofunctors"} pseudofunctors
            %strong
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
              \-weighted bilimit of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            is an object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L\in K
            equipped with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudonatural+equivalence"} pseudonatural equivalence
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi L
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi Bicat
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi D
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Cat
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi J
                  %mo ,
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi F
                  %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(X,L) \simeq Bicat(D,Cat)(J,K(X,F-)).
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Bicat
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi D
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Cat
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Bicat(D,Cat)
            denotes the 2-category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudofunctors"} pseudofunctors
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                    %mo →
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D\to Cat
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudonatural+transformations"} pseudonatural transformations
            between them, and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modifications"} modifications
            between those.
          %p
            A bilimit in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+2-category"} opposite 2-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi K
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K^{op}
            is called a
            %strong bicolimit
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
          %p
            It is also possible to require the weight
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            to go from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi D
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D^{op}
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
            and the pseudofunctor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            to go from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            when defining bicolimits, in this case a
            = succeed "-weighted" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            is an object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            equipped with a pseudonatural equivalence:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi Bicat
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi D
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Cat
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi J
                  %mo ,
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi F
                  %mo −
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(C,X) \simeq Bicat(D^{op},Cat)(J,K(F-,X)).
          %h3#Terminology Strictness and terminology
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            are
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+2-categories"} strict 2-categories
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            are
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+2-functors"} strict 2-functors
            %em and
            the 2-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Bicat
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi D
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Cat
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Bicat(D,Cat)
            by the 2-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi D
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Cat
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [D,Cat]
            of strict 2-functors and strict 2-natural transformations, then we obtain the definition of a
            = succeed "." do
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+2-limit"} strict 2-limit
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched category
            theory. See
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+2-limit"} strict 2-limit
            for details, and for other variants.
          %p
            When we know we are working in a bicategory, the only type of limit that makes sense is a bilimit. Therefore, we usually call these simply “limits”. However, in a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+2-category"} strict 2-category
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+2-limit"} strict 2-limit
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/biproduct"} completely unrelated meaning
            of an object that is both a product and a coproduct (which is common in
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/additive+category"} additive categories
          %p
            Unfortunately, we probably shouldn’t use “weak limit” to emphasize the “up-to-isomorphism” nature of these limits, because that also has the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+limit"} completely unrelated meaning
            of an object in a 1-category satisfying the existence, but not the uniqueness property of an ordinary limit.
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#bilimits_over_diagrams_of_special_shape Bilimits over diagrams of special shape
          %p
            Any ordinary type of limit can be “bicategorified” by boosting its ordinary universal property up to a bicategorical one. In the following examples we work in a bicategory
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                A
                %strong
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
                in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
                is an object 1 such that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(X,1)
                is equivalent to the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+category"} terminal category
                for any object
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                there is a morphism
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\to 1
                and for any two morphisms
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo ,
                      %mi g
                      %mo :
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f,g:X\to 1
                there is a unique morphism
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo →
                        %mi g
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\to g
            %li
              %p
                A
                %strong
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product"} product
                of two objects
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A,B
                in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
                is an object
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ×
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\times B
                together with a natural equivalence of categories
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi K
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi A
                        %mo ×
                        %mi B
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ≃
                        %mi K
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ×
                        %mi K
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi B
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(X,A\times B) \simeq K(X,A)\times K(X,B)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ×
                      %mi B
                      %mo →
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p:A\times B\to A
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi q
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ×
                      %mi B
                      %mo →
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q:A\times B\to B
                such that (1) for any
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:X\to A
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi g
                        %mo :
                        %mi X
                        %mo →
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g:X\to B
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi h
                      %mo :
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi A
                      %mo ×
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h:X\to A\times B
                and isomorphisms
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mi h
                      %mo ≅
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p h\cong f
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi q
                        %mi h
                        %mo ≅
                        %mi g
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q h\cong g
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi h
                      %mo ,
                      %mi k
                      %mo :
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi A
                      %mo ×
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h,k:X\to A\times B
                and 2-cells
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                      %mo :
                      %mi p
                      %mi h
                      %mo →
                      %mi p
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha:p h \to p k
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi β
                        %mo :
                        %mi q
                        %mi h
                        %mo →
                        %mi q
                        %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta: q h \to q k
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi γ
                      %mo :
                      %mi h
                      %mo →
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma:h \to k
                such that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mi γ
                      %mo =
                      %mi α
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \gamma = \alpha
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi q
                        %mi γ
                        %mo =
                        %mi β
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q \gamma = \beta
            %li
              %p
                A
                %strong
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
                of a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/co-span"} co-span
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mi f
                      %mi C
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mi g
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \overset{f}{\to} C \overset{g}{\leftarrow} B
                consists of an object
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %msub
                        %mo ×
                        %mi C
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\times_C B
                and projections
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %msub
                        %mo ×
                        %mi C
                      %mi B
                      %mo →
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p:A\times_C B\to A
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi q
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %msub
                        %mo ×
                        %mi C
                      %mi B
                      %mo →
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q:A\times_C B\to B
                together with an isomorphism
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mo :
                        %mi f
                        %mi p
                        %mo ≅
                        %mi g
                        %mi q
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi:f p \cong g q
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi m
                      %mo :
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m:X\to A
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo :
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n:X\to B
                with an isomorphism
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ψ
                        %mo :
                        %mi f
                        %mi m
                        %mo ≅
                        %mi g
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi:f m \cong g n
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi h
                      %mo :
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi A
                      %msub
                        %mo ×
                        %mi C
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h:X\to A\times_C B
                and isomorphisms
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                      %mo :
                      %mi p
                      %mi h
                      %mo ≅
                      %mi m
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha:p h \cong m
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi β
                      %mo :
                      %mi q
                      %mi h
                      %mo ≅
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta:q h \cong n
                such that
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi g
                        %mi β
                        %mo .
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mi h
                        %mo .
                        %mi f
                        %msup
                          %mi α
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                        %mo =
                        %mi ψ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g\beta . \phi h . f \alpha^{-1} = \psi
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi h
                      %mo ,
                      %mi k
                      %mo :
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi A
                      %msub
                        %mo ×
                        %mi C
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h,k:X\to A\times_C B
                and 2-cells
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi μ
                      %mo :
                      %mi p
                      %mi h
                      %mo →
                      %mi p
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu:p h \to p k
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ν
                      %mo :
                      %mi q
                      %mi h
                      %mo →
                      %mi q
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nu:q h \to q k
                such that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mi μ
                      %mo =
                      %mi g
                      %mi ν
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \mu = g \nu
                (modulo the given isomorphism
                = succeed ")," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mi p
                        %mo ≅
                        %mi g
                        %mi q
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f p \cong g q
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mi k
                        %mo .
                        %mi f
                        %mi μ
                        %mo =
                        %mi g
                        %mi ν
                        %mo .
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mi h
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi k . f\mu = g\nu . \phi h
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi γ
                      %mo :
                      %mi h
                      %mo →
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma:h\to k
                such that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mi γ
                      %mo =
                      %mi μ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \gamma = \mu
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi q
                        %mi γ
                        %mo =
                        %mi ν
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q \gamma = \nu
                %em pseudo-pullback
                but that term more properly refers to a particular
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+2-limit"} strict 2-limit
            %li
              %p
                An
                %strong
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equalizer"} equalizer
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo ,
                      %mi g
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f,g:A\to B
                consists of an object
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
                and a morphism
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi e
                      %mo :
                      %mi E
                      %mo →
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e:E\to A
                together with an isomorphism
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mi e
                        %mo ≅
                        %mi g
                        %mi e
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f e \cong g e
                %em pseudo-equalizer
                but that term more properly refers to a particular
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+2-limit"} strict 2-limit
                = succeed "s." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent+object"} descent object
          %p There are also various important types of bilimits that involve 2-cells in the diagram shape or in the weight, and hence are not just “boosted-up” versions of 1-limits.
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                The
                %strong
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comma+object"} comma object
                of a cospan
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mi f
                      %mi C
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mi g
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \overset{f}{\to} C \overset{g}{\leftarrow} B
                is a universal object
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f/g)
                and projections
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo :
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p:(f/g)\to A
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi q
                      %mo :
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q:(f/g)\to B
                together with a transformation (not an isomorphism)
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mi p
                        %mo →
                        %mi g
                        %mi q
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f p \to g q
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comma+objects"} comma objects
                are
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comma+category"} comma categories
                %em lax pullbacks
                but that term more properly refers to the lax version of a pullback; see “lax limits” below.
            %li
              %p
                The
                %strong
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inserter"} inserter
                of a pair of parallel arrows
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo ,
                      %mi g
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ⇉
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f,g:A \;\rightrightarrows\; B
                is a universal object
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
                equipped with a map
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo :
                      %mi I
                      %mo →
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i:I\to A
                and a 2-cell
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mi i
                        %mo →
                        %mi g
                        %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f i \to g i
            %li
              %p
                The
                %strong
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equifier"} equifier
                of a pair of parallel 2-cells
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                      %mo ,
                      %mi β
                      %mo :
                      %mi f
                      %mo →
                      %mi g
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha,\beta: f\to g: A\to B
                is a universal object
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
                equipped with a map
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi e
                      %mo :
                      %mi E
                      %mo →
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e:E\to A
                such that
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi α
                        %mi e
                        %mo =
                        %mi β
                        %mi e
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha e = \beta e
            %li
              %p
                The
                %strong
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverter"} inverter
                of a 2-cell
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                      %mo :
                      %mi f
                      %mo →
                      %mi g
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha:f\to g:A\to B
                is a universal object
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                with a map
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi v
                      %mo :
                      %mi V
                      %mo →
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v:V\to A
                such that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                      %mi v
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha v
                is invertible.
            %li
              %p
                The
                %strong
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power"} power
                of an object
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                by a category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                is a universal object
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi A
                        %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^C
                equipped with a functor
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                        %mo →
                        %mi K
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi A
                          %mi C
                        %mo ,
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C\to K(A^C,A)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/walking+arrow"} walking arrow
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{2}
          %h3#finite_bilimits Finite biLimits
          %p
            A bilimit is called
            %strong finite
            if its diagram shape and its weight are both “finitely presentable” in a suitable sense (defined in terms of
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/computads"} computads
            %a{:href => "#StreetLimitsIndexed"} Street’s article
            %em Limits indexed by category-valued 2-functors
            ). Pullbacks, comma objects, inserters, equifiers, and so on are all finite limits, as are powers by any finitely presented category. All finite limits can be constructed from pullbacks, a terminal object, and powers with
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{2}
          %h3{:id => "(2,1)limit"}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (2,1)
            \-limits
          %p
            If the ambient
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicategory"} bicategory
            is in fact a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%282%2C1%29-category"} (2,1)-category
            in that all
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-morphism"} 2-morphism
            %strong
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (2,1)
              \-limits
            and
            %strong
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (2,1)
              \-colimits
            in this case.
          %p
            These are then a special case of the more general
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-limit"} (∞,1)-limit
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-colimit"} (∞,1)-colimit
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%282%2C1%29-category"} (2,1)-category
            is a special case of an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
          %p
            Traditionally,
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-limit"} (∞,1)-limit
            = succeed "-categories" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories+with+weak+equivalences"} categories with weak equivalences
            in general and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+categories"} model categories
            in particular. (2,1)-limits can often also be viewed in this way. The corresponding presentation of the
            = succeed "-limits" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            = succeed "-limits" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (2,1)
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+limit"}> homotopy limit
              s
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+colimit"}> homotopy colimit
                s
          %p
            For instance bilimits in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%282%2C1%29-category"} (2,1)-category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grpd"} Grpd
            of
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+limit"} homotopy limit
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} model structure on simplicial sets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi sSet
                    %mi Quillen
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet_{Quillen}
            of diagrams of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-truncated"} 1-truncated
            = succeed "es." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
            = succeed "-limits" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-limit"} (∞,1)-limit
          %p
            Or for instance, more generally, the bilimits in any
            = succeed "(=" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%282%2C1%29-sheaf"} (2,1)-sheaf
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stack"} stack
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%282%2C1%29-topos"} (2,1)-topos
            may be computed as
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+limit"} homotopy limit
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} model structure on simplicial presheaves
            over the given
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%282%2C1%29-site"} (2,1)-site
            of diagrams of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-truncated"} 1-truncated
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+presheaves"} simplicial presheaves
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/big+topos"} big (2,1)-toposes
            such as those over the large sites
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SmoothMfd"} SmoothMfd
            where computations with
            = succeed "s/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+groupoid"} topological groupoid
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+stack"} topological stack
            = succeed "s/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groupoid"} Lie groupoid
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentiable+stack"} differentiable stack
          %h3#lax Lax limits
          %p
            A
            %strong lax limit
            can be defined like a bilimit, except that the triangles in the definition of a cone are required only to commute up to a specified
            = succeed "," do
              %em transformation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Bicat
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi D
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Cat
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Bicat(D,Cat)
            we use the 2-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Bicat
                    %mi l
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi D
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Cat
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Bicat_l(D,Cat)
            whose morphisms are
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax+natural+transformations"} lax natural transformations
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            of a diagram
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            weighted by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            is equipped with a universal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax+natural+transformation"} lax natural transformation
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                    %mo →
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi L
                    %mo ,
                    %mi F
                    %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J\to K(L,F-)
          %p
            This may look like a different concept, but in fact, for any weight
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            there is another weight
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Q
                    %mi l
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi J
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q_l(J)
            such that
            = succeed "-weighted" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            = succeed "-weighted" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Q
                      %mi l
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi J
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q_l(J)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Q
                    %mi l
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q_l
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax+morphism+classifier"} lax morphism classifier
            for pseudofunctors. Therefore, lax limits are really a special case of bilimits. Similarly,
            = succeed "," do
              %strong oplax limits
          %p
            There is a further simplification of lax limits in the case of “conical” lax limits where the weight
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                  %mo =
                  %mi Δ
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J=\Delta 1
            is constant at the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+category"} terminal category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Δ
                  %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi F
                  %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta 1 \to K(X,F-)
            is the same as a lax natural transformation
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta X \to F
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            is a representing object for such lax transformations.
          %p Here are some examples.
          %ul
            %li
              %p Lax terminal objects and lax products are the same as ordinary ones, since there are no commutativity conditions on the cones.
            %li
              %p
                The
                %strong lax bilimit of an arrow
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:A\to B
                is a universal object
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi L
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
                equipped with projections
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo :
                      %mi L
                      %mo →
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p:L\to A
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi q
                      %mo :
                      %mi L
                      %mo →
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q:L\to B
                and a 2-cell
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mi p
                        %mo →
                        %mi q
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f p \to q
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %msub
                          %mn 1
                          %mi B
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f/1_B)
            %li
              %p
                The
                %strong lax pullback
                of a cospan
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mi f
                      %mi C
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mi g
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \overset{f}{\to} C \overset{g}{\leftarrow} B
                is a universal object
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
                equipped with projections
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo :
                        %mi P
                        %mo →
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p:P\to A
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi q
                        %mo :
                        %mi P
                        %mo →
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q:P\to B
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi r
                        %mo :
                        %mi P
                        %mo →
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r:P\to C
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mi p
                      %mo →
                      %mi r
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f p \to r
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi g
                        %mi q
                        %mo →
                        %mi r
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g q \to r
          %p
            Note that lax pullbacks are
            %em not
            the same as
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comma+objects"} comma objects
          %p
            A
            %strong lax bicolimit
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            is, of course, a lax bilimit in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi K
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K^{op}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax+natural+transformations"} lax natural transformations
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                    %mo →
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mo −
                    %mo ,
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J \to K(F-,L)
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                    %mo =
                    %mi Δ
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J=\Delta 1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Δ
                  %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi F
                  %mo −
                  %mo ,
                  %mi L
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta 1 \to K(F-,L)
            is the same as an
            %em oplax
            natural transformation
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo →
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \to \Delta L
          .un_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              With this in mind, one might be tempted to switch the meanings of “lax bicolimit” and “oplax bicolimit”, but there is a good reason not to. Recall that a lax
              = succeed "-weighted" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
              = succeed "-weighted" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Q
                        %mi l
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi J
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q_l(J)
              = succeed "-weighted" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              is the same as a
              = succeed "-weighted" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi K
                        %mi op
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K^{op}
              = succeed "-weighted" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              should be an ordinary
              = succeed "-weighted" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Q
                        %mi l
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi J
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q_l(J)
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              = succeed "-weighted" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Q
                        %mi l
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi J
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q_l(J)
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi K
                        %mi op
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K^{op}
              = succeed "-weighted" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi K
                        %mi op
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K^{op}
          %p Here are some examples of lax and oplax bicolimits:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                A
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kleisli+object"} Kleisli object
                is a lax bicolimit of a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            %li
              %p
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/collage"} collage
                of a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/profunctor"} profunctor
                is its lax bicolimit, regarded as a diagram in the 2-category
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Prof"} Prof
            %li
              %p
                When
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                is a category, the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+construction"} Grothendieck construction
                of a functor
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo →
                      %mi Cat
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C\to Cat
                is the same as its
                %em oplax
                bicolimit; see
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Grothendieck+construction#AsALaxColimit"} here
          %h3#2ColimitsInCat
            2-Colimits in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
          %p
            As shown
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Grothendieck+construction#AsALaxColimit"} here
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is an ordinary category and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \colon C \to Cat
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudofunctor"} pseudofunctor
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/oplax+colimit"} oplax colimit
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            is given by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+construction"} Grothendieck construction
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∫
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \int F
            — and its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudo-colimit"} pseudo-colimit
            is given by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization"} formally inverting
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+morphism"} opcartesian
            morphisms in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∫
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \int F
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
          %p
            Moreover, a similar result holds more generally when
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicategory"} bicategory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∫
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \int F
            is also a bicategory: a 2-cell from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi m
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi c
                  %mo →
                  %mi d
                  %mo ,
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msub
                    %mi m
                    %mo *
                  %mi x
                  %mo →
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (m \colon c \to d, f \colon m_*x \to y)
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi c
                  %mo →
                  %mi d
                  %mo ,
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msub
                    %mi n
                    %mo *
                  %mi x
                  %mo →
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n \colon c \to d, g \colon n_*x \to y)
            is given by a 2-cell
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi μ
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi m
                  %mo ⇒
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu \colon m \Rightarrow n
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi μ
                    %mo *
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu_* x
            is a morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo →
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \to g
            over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_*
            denote the functor that sends a bicategory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            to the category whose objects are those of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            and whose hom-sets are the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+category"} connected components
            of the hom-categories of
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_*
            denote the functor that sends a category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to the corresponding locally discrete bicategory. Then there is an equivalence of categories
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi K
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mo *
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ≃
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mo *
                  %mi K
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [K, d_* X] \simeq [\pi_* K, X]
          %p It is straightforward to check that the first of the above facts extends to the bicategorical case:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Lax
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi F
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Δ
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mo ∫
                  %mi F
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mo *
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Lax(F, \Delta X) \simeq [{\textstyle \int} F, d_* X]
          %p
            as does the fact that a lax transformation on the left is pseudo if and only if the corresponding functor on the right inverts the opcartesian morphisms in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∫
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \int F
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mo *
                  %mo ⊣
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_* \dashv d_*
            holds when restricted to the functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [-, -]_{S^{-1}}
            that takes two categories or bicategories to the full subcategory of functors that invert the class
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            of morphisms. Taking
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            to be the opcartesian morphisms in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∫
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \int F
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ps
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi F
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Δ
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mo ∫
                  %mi F
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mo *
                  %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                  %mo ≃
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mo *
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mo ∫
                  %mi F
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                  %mo ≃
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mo *
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mo ∫
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Ps(F, \Delta X) \simeq [{\textstyle \int} F, d_* X]_{S^{-1}}
                  \\simeq [\pi_* {\textstyle \int} F, X]_{S^{-1}}
                  \\simeq [(\pi_* {\textstyle \int} F)[S^{-1}], X]
          %p
            Hence the pseudo colimit of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            is got by taking its
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicategory+of+elements"} bicategory of elements
            = succeed "\u2019" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
